## Main Win

The biggest win today was slowing down and really understanding the browser interaction flow:

1. Select an HTML element with `document.getElementById()`
2. Attach a click listener with `addEventListener()`
3. Run a callback function when the button is clicked
4. Use `prompt()` to collect user input
5. Display the result back on the page with `textContent`

Example pattern:

```js
const btn = document.getElementById("prompt-btn");
const output = document.getElementById("output");

btn.addEventListener("click", () => {
  const userName = prompt("What is your name?");
  output.textContent = `Hello, ${userName}, keep up the great work!`;
});
